  "core": "Compassion feels what another feels and moves toward them. In Nurturing, it works on the structure that holds and feeds — the ground-keeping, the slow tending. Overdone, the feeling floods the structure: someone else's weight pours into the space the holding needed, and carrying them replaces the tending. The nourishment turns into absorption.",
  "sheetLine": "Someone else's hunger filled the ground; the feeding has turned into being fed upon."
